+#   schedpolicy: sets process scheduling policies (sched_setscheduler/sched_getparam), which Zephyr does not support
+#   sctp: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   seal: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   seccomp: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   secretmem: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   sem-sysv: System V IPC (semget) is not provided
+#   sendfile: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   shm-sysv: System V IPC (shmget) is not provided
+#   sigbus: offered once a user-mode fault generates a signal
+#   sigfd: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   sigfpe: offered once a user-mode fault generates a signal
+#   sigill: offered once a user-mode fault generates a signal
+#   sigio: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   signest: sigaction(SIGWINCH) fails: the kernel numbers no SIGWINCH (added by POSIX.1-2024)
+#   sigsegv: offered once a user-mode fault generates a signal
+#   sigtrap: offered once a user-mode fault generates a signal
+#   sigurg: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   sigvtalrm: needs setitimer (XSI_TIMERS), not implemented yet
+#   sigxcpu: needs getrlimit/setrlimit (XSI_MULTI_PROCESS), not implemented yet
+#   sigxfsz: needs getrlimit/setrlimit (XSI_MULTI_PROCESS), not implemented yet
+#   smi: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   sockdiag: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   sockfd: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   spawn: refuses to run as root, and Zephyr processes are uid 0
+#   splice: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   stack: offered once XSI_SIGNALS provides sigaltstack()
+#   stackmmap: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux system-call exerciser
+#   statmount: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   strnum: verifies long double scanf precision; picolibc's %Lf scanf is not exact
+#   swap: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   sync-file: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   sysbadaddr: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux system-call exerciser
+#   syscall: Linux system call coverage exerciser
+#   sysfs: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   sysinval: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux system-call exerciser
+#   tee: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   timerfd: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   tlb-numa: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   tlb-shootdown: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   tmpfs: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   tun: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   udp-flood: floods INADDR_ANY, a Linux loopback shortcut Zephyr's stack rejects
+#   umask: offered once the file attributes group stores modes and owners
+#   umount: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   unshare: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   uprobe: stress-ng builds it as unimplemented on Zephyr: Linux-only interfaces
+#   urandom: needs /dev/random and /dev/urandom, which Zephyr does not populate
